{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212187-brainstorming-for-a-dark-era-about-the-birth-of-psychoanalysis","id":1212187,"title":"Brainstorming for a Dark Era about the birth of Psychoanalysis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-27T02:47:33-07:00","id":1212187,"title":"Brainstorming for a Dark Era about the birth of Psychoanalysis","content":"Hey there.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking for a while about a Dark Era focused on the birth of psychoanalysis. Namely, one that's mostly about Freud, Jung, the revolution their theories caused and that plays with monsters, mental health, dreams and the clash between supernatural and science, all seasoned with the mood and events of late 19th-early 20th century Central Europe. Mostly focused on Austria and Switzerland for obvious reasons, though mention of other places would appear when appropriate. After all, the Era is more based around a scientific movement rather than a series of localized events.<br /> <br /> Like all ideas that won't leave my mind, I made peace with the fact that I'm eventually going to try and write it. It's gonna be <i>really </i>far in the future, since I have a long list of things to do before that (including finishing another Dark Era when Geist comes out) and I have no intention whatsoever to dedicate myself to a lengthy project like that right now, but experience taught me these things require careful planning and research, so I'm starting to gather some toughts. Besides, I have plenty of books about Freud, Jung and psychoanalysis, but I'm gonna need more than that for a Dark Era.<br /> <br /> This brings me here asking for ideas, suggestions and opinions. Truth be told, it will be a Beast Dark Era at the very least, because that's from where the idea came and I think I can do something decent and interesting with the tools and hooks the gameline provides in this context, But, pitch for Beast or not, I'm posting this in the general forum because I could use any sort of comment and because the template for Dark Eras now generally includes more than one gameline. So, I'm open to suggestions.<br /> <br /> What you think this Era should cover? Any sort of elements that can't be missing? Others that should? Which gamelines you'd like for it to include? Basically anything you think can be useful to discuss is welcome. As the title says, this is a brainstorming thread, so there are no wrong replies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-27-2018, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T03:49:56-07:00","id":1212197,"title":"","content":"I could see Mage(and the Astral/Goetia impact) represented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:57:37-07:00","id":1212226,"title":"","content":"Aside from the obvious (Beast and Mage)....<br /> <br /> Vampires dissecting the Beast in their own heads. The Ordo will be interested. <br /> Werewolves exploring their own Kuruth, and the effects of Lunacy. <br /> Prometheans trying to alleviate their Torment and figure out how human minds work. <br /> Changelings incorporating psychoanalysis to oneiromancy and Hedgespinning. <br /> The Bound, especially Sin-Eaters, diving deep into the minds of the dead, seeing if there\u2019s a way to make them Pass On. <br /> Demons hacking into the psychological subroutines of humanity to mitigate Compromise, while angels invoke said subroutines to create sleeper agents. <br /> Mummies seeing how pale the modern world\u2019s science of the soul is compared to that of Irem, yet finding new breakthroughs to reflect on their Pillars.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and Dreamers from CofD core. Maybe they can get an expansion instead of the other supernaturals, like how Skinchangers got one in Dark Eras. And of course, for something more classic, the Infernal host has a thing or two to say about what\u2019s lurking in the hearts of men...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-27-2018, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:42:03-07:00","id":1212329,"title":"","content":"Seconding Mage, and I think this could be a very interesting era in which to explore Changeling. Not just for the oneiromancy, but also because changelings are all inherently pretty traumatized, and the root of all this psychoanalysis stuff was to help the mentally ill, whether or not it actually did. I could see an Entitlement of changeling psychoanalysts trying to work out new ways of restoring Clarity, and perhaps a rival Entitlement (or a group of Loyalists) arguing that changelings only got taken because they subconsciously wanted to be enslaved and other victim-blaming nonsense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:50:22-07:00","id":1212335,"title":"","content":"The Eigner Lodge is a lodge of Cahalith that latched on to Freuds (and later Jungs) ideas regarding dream analysis in the 1920s (Cahalith being incessantly plagued by prophetic dreams from Luna and her choir). They have a clinic now though before it became a lodge it was a 'salon' in Vienna. While dream analysis is their main thing they seem to help a lot with people who had rough First Changes, especially those who are still parts of families whose guardians think their children need therapy.<br /> <br /> They're described in Signs of the Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-27-2018, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:37:21-07:00","id":1212432,"title":"","content":"If it's going to centre on Freud, it should be for three splats, to go with the Id, Ego, and Superego. The superego is the conscience, sort of - the collection of rules and ideals a person thinks they should abide by - which corresponds to Beasts' lessons in a supremely fucked up way. The id is irrational desire without the ability to compare impulse to reality - that lack of clarity is something changelings have to deal with, and deep primal emotions fit with how the Courts organise. And the ego is kind of an unconscious rationality - which could work with Mage. Those three also allow the Primordial Dream, Astral, and Skein to combined into one vast payground where all of Jung's archetypes can hold sway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:14:18-07:00","id":1212459,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the British Society of the Twelve Keys, the forerunner of the Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit, formed during the Ripper murders, from Hunter, and how Teleinformatics might work with psychoanalysis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T17:14:45-07:00","id":1212498,"title":"","content":"Hmm, picking which gamelines to cover sure is shaping up to be a tough choice. Thanks everyone, keep these coming, they're quite helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T08:30:43-07:00","id":1212675,"title":"","content":"I'd vote for Changeling and Beast as the primary game lines to explore. If you wanted to include more than two, maybe Geist or Mage. I lean in the direction of Changeling and Beast mostly because of their strong connection to Jungian concepts like universal archetypes, dream interpretation and the &quot;shadow self.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's an aspect of the birth of psychoanalysis that isn't often talked about<b></b>: When Freud started practicing his talking cure, he was working primarily with one specific group of patients: young women from wealthy families who were experiencing &quot;hysteria&quot; (what's now called &quot;conversion disorder&quot;): the presence of physical symptoms without a physical cause. Through talking with these women and exploring the nature and genesis of their symptoms, he came to a conclusion: that in the overwhelming majority of these cases, the young woman in question was being sexually abused (generally by her father). When he went to publish these findings, he was rebuked by his publisher and told that his conclusion must be faulty, as it was impossible that the well-to-do men of Vienna might sexually abuse their daughters. So, rather than standing his ground, he went back to his office and worked come up with some theory for why young women might -think- they had been sexually abused by their fathers. What he came up with were some of the concepts he is now best known for: ideas like penis envy and the Oedipus complex. So, to sum up, the dark history of psychoanalysis includes a compromise that covered up for sexual abusers and did real harm to psychological practice with women for decades.<br /> <br /> When constructing your setting, you might put some thought into what to make of this aspect of the period. It would be easy enough to say that Freud learned <b>something else</b> through his work with symptomatic young women and had to cover it up. Personally, I would say the respectful thing to do would be to leave the history as it is: a chilling example of an educated man covering up the real causes of women's trauma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:08:18-07:00","id":1212742,"title":"","content":"...You know. Taking that into account, that sounds chillingly like what Deviant has been described as to us so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:47:43-07:00","id":1212757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212187-brainstorming-for-a-dark-era-about-the-birth-of-psychoanalysis?p=1212742#post1212742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...You know. Taking that into account, that sounds chillingly like what Deviant has been described as to us so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't be sure until we know more, but Deviant seems like having lot of potential here. It's one of the checkpoints I'm waiting for before getting to work.<br /> <br /> As for giving supernatural explanation to human behaviors, I'm generally more of the idea of leaving them as is, so we do agree on that. Not saying in not gonna intertwine things here and there, that's the whole point, but I do believe that real screw-ups and crimes are better done if the responsibilty remains mostly untouched from the supernatural. Reality is already scary and chilling as it is, to deny the truth of the events would be a disservice to both history and readers.<br /> <br /> I tend to prefer letting monsters do their own thing and be the one influenced by men (and just then influence in return). And remember that CotD monsters are people before the supernatural template happens. It's a method that served me well when writing about that minefield of horror that's Belgian Congo, and I doubt I'm gonna shy away from Freud's (or anyone else) mistakes and the fault of the society of the time here either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-28-2018, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:16:02-07:00","id":1212864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212187-brainstorming-for-a-dark-era-about-the-birth-of-psychoanalysis?p=1212757#post1212757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt I'm gonna shy away from Freud's (or anyone else) mistakes and the fault of the society of the time here either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good plan, though Sde Spencer's idea is worth following up for the Deviant section if there is one - psychoanalysis would be an unusual science to use for a Remade's origin. On reflection, I also concur with gscrap's idea over my own - Beast and Changeling - I still like the dream-/soulscape as a vast psychological tapestry, but Beasts and changelings are at the opposite ends of it - leaving Mage out of the main lineup leaves the Astral in between as an known territory for both species to explore, just as the mind is being explored in the mortal world around them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T00:09:41-07:00","id":1212967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212187-brainstorming-for-a-dark-era-about-the-birth-of-psychoanalysis?p=1212432#post1212432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's going to centre on Freud, it should be for three splats, to go with the Id, Ego, and Superego. The superego is the conscience, sort of - the collection of rules and ideals a person thinks they should abide by - which corresponds to Beasts' lessons in a supremely fucked up way. The id is irrational desire without the ability to compare impulse to reality - that lack of clarity is something changelings have to deal with, and deep primal emotions fit with how the Courts organise. And the ego is kind of an unconscious rationality - which could work with Mage. Those three also allow the Primordial Dream, Astral, and Skein to combined into one vast payground where all of Jung's archetypes can hold sway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally support splitting Era supernatural material in to Id = Changelings, Ego = Mages and Superego = Beasts. It's really cool use of Era's main real world theory itself. ( Well, maybe switching Beast for Id, Changeling for Ego and Mages for Superego - as Beasts are much more about primal desires of their Horrors and Mages could work with Superego as Hubris, but it's a bit academic discussion here. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T00:20:24-07:00","id":1212972,"title":"","content":"Depending how long you want to dwell into 20th century, <b>Cinder</b> - remember that in Mage we have whole theosophical thing coming out. Stressing <i>Superego = Hubris</i> theme, I point that from <b>MtAw</b> canon, Thule in Germany - that inspired Nazis - was supported from radical part of Mysterium, called<i> Jnanamukti </i>- this is what Orderbook have on them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mysterium, page 82</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It began as a society of Mysterium mages with a deep interest in theosophy. In 1929, members disseminated a controversial work called <i>The Three Enemies</i> throughout the order. Mystagogues believe that the faction reacted to the actions of the theosophical messiah, Jiddu Krishnamurti, a year before. Krish-namurti renounced the mantle of \u201cWorld Teacher,\u201d and shattered a pillar of theosophical belief.<br /> <br /> The Jnanamukti (\u201cFist of Wisdom\u201d) had been committed to synthesizing a universal philosophy and religion from theosophy and other multicultural sources in the belief that truly Atlantean teachings would reveal themselves in the common elements of many belief systems. The call to arms in The Three Enemies represented a radical reversal. The Jnanamukti now supported an apocalyptic agenda, devoted to nothing less than the downfall of Quiescent civilization. They said that worldly culture was the metaphysical enemy of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:12:38-07:00","id":1217114,"title":"","content":"The new <b>Alienist</b> TV series looks like thing that can be inspirational on the mood of opening of this Dark Era. It's year 1896 in New York and 'Alienist' studies mind of first unknown kind of killer...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q9867sT-Y1M\" data-code=\"q9867sT-Y1M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/q9867sT-Y1M/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T02:51:40-07:00","id":1217310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamst